    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1990-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(t=\\log_yx.\\) Then \\[ t+\\frac1t=\\frac{10}{3}, \\] so \\(3t^2-10t+3=0,\\) giving \\(t=3\\) or \\(\\frac{1}{3}.\\) Thus one of \\(x,y\\) is the cube of the other. Let the smaller be \\(u.\\) Then \\(u^4=xy=144,\\) so \\(u=2\\sqrt3\\) and \\(u^3=24\\sqrt3.\\) Therefore \\[ \\frac{x+y}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt3+24\\sqrt3}{2}=13\\sqrt3. \\]\n\nThus the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(t=\\log_yx,\\) so that \\(\\log_xy=\\frac{1}{t}\\)",
        "The resulting values of \\(t\\) show that one of \\(x,y\\) is the cube of the other"
      ],
